// ==UserScript==
// @name         Argon Survey Guard v13.5 (Access Control + Quiet Mode)
// @namespace    http://tampermonkey.net/
// !!! NEVER CHANGE @name OR @namespace AGAIN. Tampermonkey ties the saved data (Access ID, name, locks) to them.
// !!! A new @name = a NEW script = NEW Access ID + empty storage. Only change @version.
// @version      16.48
// @updateURL    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rohimgpt/argon-list/main/argon.user.js
// @downloadURL  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rohimgpt/argon-list/main/argon.user.js
// @description  Locks a completed survey for 7/15/30 days, tracks real start-to-end time, merge-able backups, admin-controlled remote blocklist (domains / keywords / logo images, also checked inside page links, headers, titles & logos), and an approval system (Pending / Allowed / Blocked access IDs). v16.48: UserTesting completed only via Lootwalls status=completed. v16.47: UserTesting one-page surveys are completed through Lootwalls status=completed (no thank-you text rule). v16.45: participant.use2.usertesting.com is a topic host (like ShopperMX). v16.44: UserTesting qualify page is not completed; nsv.netr.jp topic host. v16.43: better topic detection (brand names, purchase phrases, platform words ignored, word-order/plural-proof keys on Upside+ShopperMX). v16.42: Upside=start.dig.one, ShopperMX=incontext.decipherinc.com, link/id ignored, topic required. v16.41: Upside+ShopperMX strict topic matching (per-survey ratio, generic keys ignored). v16.40: topic from first 4 non-profile pages (all surveys), topic-first repeat check, 1-page surveys. v16.39: Upside topic. v16.38: repeat detected by topic when the link/id changes. v16.37: sheet has survey links only (no Lootwalls / UT screener rows). v16.36: CSV hides apiKey/userId. v16.35: UserTesting screener/legal steps no longer logged as completed. v16.34: strict-keyword and storage-lock fixes. v16.12: fixed scan crash (null.startsWith) that stopped NEW-survey alerts; admin block screen now replaces the whole page so the red screen always shows.
// @match        *://*/*
// @noframes
// @grant        GM_setValue
// @grant        GM_getValue
// @grant        GM_getTab
// @grant        GM_saveTab
// @grant        GM_registerMenuCommand
// @grant        GM_unregisterMenuCommand
// @grant        GM_notification
// @grant        GM_xmlhttpRequest
// @grant        GM_openInTab
// @connect      raw.githubusercontent.com
// @connect      api.github.com
// @connect      argon-track.mdsam7997.workers.dev
// @connect      *
// @run-at       document-start
// ==/UserScript==
// SECURITY NOTE: network is used ONLY to (a) download the admin list (plain JSON data, never executed)
// (b) the manual "Check for update" menu item (reads the @version line of the script file only),
// (c) employee work report to your own server (client ID, employee name, access status, per survey: domain + duration; no full URLs / questions / answers), only if TRACK_URL is set (one report every 6 hours),
// (d) for the admin only: publish changes to that JSON file via the GitHub API, and read the report data from your own server,
// (e) v15.5: read-only GET of logo images (cross-origin) so a pixel fingerprint can be computed. Images are never executed or uploaded.
// No @require, no @resource, no eval.

